WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.134 --> 00:00:19.343
After a long sleep, Rat awoke.

2
00:00:19.344 --> 00:00:21.765
He sat up in his chair.

3
00:00:21.766 --> 00:00:24.740
"You look much better," said Mole.

4
00:00:24.741 --> 00:00:28.407
Rat's eyes were clear again.

5
00:00:28.408 --> 00:00:32.404
"What happened to you?" asked Mole.

6
00:00:32.405 --> 00:00:35.277
"You almost left the riverbank!"

7
00:00:35.278 --> 00:00:38.306
"I don't know," said Rat.

8
00:00:38.307 --> 00:00:40.605
"It's hard to say."

9
00:00:40.606 --> 00:00:44.475
Rat told Mole about the visitor.

10
00:00:44.476 --> 00:00:48.272
"I listened to Sea Rat," said Rat.

11
00:00:48.273 --> 00:00:51.475
"His story was like a dream.

12
00:00:51.476 --> 00:00:55.275
I acted as if I wasn't awake."

13
00:00:55.276 --> 00:00:58.942
"How very strange," said Mole.

14
00:00:58.943 --> 00:01:03.809
"Now, I feel sad," said Rat.

15
00:01:03.810 --> 00:01:08.012
"Rat, you'll be happy again," said Mole.

16
00:01:08.013 --> 00:01:10.126
"Just look outside."

17
00:01:10.127 --> 00:01:12.469
"Why?" asked Rat.

18
00:01:12.470 --> 00:01:16.802
"The apples are red," said Mole.

19
00:01:16.803 --> 00:01:20.339
"Nuts are falling from the trees.

20
00:01:20.340 --> 00:01:22.340
The pumpkins are fat!"

21
00:01:22.341 --> 00:01:26.343
"I'm feeling a little better," said Rat.

22
00:01:26.344 --> 00:01:29.800
Mole went to get Rat's notebook.

23
00:01:29.801 --> 00:01:32.152
He found a pencil too.

24
00:01:32.153 --> 00:01:34.406
"Here, Rat," said Mole.

25
00:01:34.407 --> 00:01:37.803
"You haven't written in a long time."

26
00:01:37.804 --> 00:01:41.695
"I don't want to," said Rat.

27
00:01:41.696 --> 00:01:45.012
He pushed the notebook and pencil away.

28
00:01:45.013 --> 00:01:48.469
"I'll let you rest some more," said Mole.

29
00:01:48.470 --> 00:01:52.477
Mole set the notebook on the table.

30
00:01:52.478 --> 00:01:57.561
After Mole left, Rat picked up the pencil.

31
00:01:57.562 --> 00:02:00.491
He sat with the notebook on his knee.

32
00:02:00.492 --> 00:02:04.478
Then Rat started a new poem.

33
00:02:04.479 --> 00:02:11.636
"Home Sweet Home," he wrote.
